id: pm-j8spis
title: Resume due telemetry after a concurrent background upload
description: "A real source get finish remained queued for432.545 seconds until a later invocation, though it eventually paired. The detached worker flushes one snapshot; a concurrent completion can append after that snapshot while its foreground scheduling is refused by the active flush lock. Reconcile and schedule due tail work after releasing that lock, without foreground network I/O, busy retries, or recreating removed storage."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: delivery,sdk,telemetry
created_at: "2026-10-13T16:48:11.966Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T20:01:01.660Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-13T20:01:00.875Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-13T20:01:00.875Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: A deterministic real-SDK worker collector receives a finish appended during the first POST without a subsequent user command; future-backoff work does not spin; disabled consent or removed storage cannot restart workers; event and OTLP tail work are covered; existing SDK/CLI performance and security gates pass.
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Continue due detached event/span draining after each released upload lock, recheck consent and identity, stop stagnant or future-retry work, and snapshot artifacts independently so one unreadable queue cannot block healthy delivery"
expected_result: Completions appended during uploads deliver without another command and each healthy artifact drains independently without recreating removed storage or foreground network I/O
actual_result: "Pre-correction real tail control times out and both unreadable-artifact controls deliver nothing; corrected158-case telemetry suite,10399-case full coverage with exact100percent in all4 dimensions, typecheck/lint/secrets and9 packed consumers pass; failed prior prerequisites remain preserved and final hosted/review admission is required"
